recitals:
WHEREAS, the Service Provider is a leading provider of cloud-based SaaS solutions in India, offering scalable, secure, and compliant infrastructure for businesses;

WHEREAS, the Customer requires a robust, high-availability SaaS platform to support its retail operations, including data storage, analytics, and customer engagement tools;

WHEREAS, both parties agree that the services to be provided under this Agreement shall comply with the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (DPDPA), the Information Technology Act, 2000 (IT Act), and all other applicable Indian laws and regulations;

WHEREAS, the Customer retains 100% ownership of all data uploaded to the Service Provider’s platform, and the Service Provider shall not claim any rights over such data except as expressly provided herein;

WHEREAS, the Service Provider undertakes to provide services with a monthly uptime commitment of 99.9%, with graduated service credits for downtime as specified in Section [X] (Scope of Services);

WHEREAS, both parties desire to enter into this Agreement to formalize their relationship and define the terms and conditions governing the provision of services.

services_provided:
Hosting and management of the Customer’s SaaS platform on the Service Provider’s cloud infrastructure;

Providing 24x7 technical support and troubleshooting for the Customer’s platform;

Ensuring compliance with DPDPA 2023, IT Act 2000, and all other applicable Indian laws and regulations;

Developing and maintaining custom applications and integrations as specified in the Annexure [X] (Service Schedule);

Providing data analytics, reporting, and insights based on the Customer’s Data, as outlined in the Annexure [X].

process.details:
Each invoice shall include:
- The invoice number and date;
- A detailed breakdown of the Services provided;
- The applicable Service Fees and any applicable taxes;
- The payment terms and due date;
- The bank details for payment.

mutual_indemnification.description:
Each party shall indemnify, defend, and hold harmless the other party from and against any claims, damages, liabilities, losses, or expenses (including reasonable attorneys’ fees) arising out of or related to:
- Any breach of intellectual property rights by the indemnifying party;
- Any infringement of third-party intellectual property rights caused by the indemnifying party’s Confidential Information or Custom Deliverables.

effect_of_termination.surviving_provisions:
The following provisions shall survive termination:
- Confidentiality (Section [X]);
- Indemnification (Section [X]);
- Intellectual Property (Section [X]);
- Dispute Resolution (Section [X]);
- Governing Law and Jurisdiction (Section [X]).

service_provider_indemnification.description:
The Service Provider shall indemnify, defend, and hold harmless the Customer from and against any claims, damages, liabilities, losses, or expenses (including reasonable attorneys’ fees) arising out of or related to:
- Any breach of the Service Provider’s warranties under Section [X];
- Any infringement of third-party intellectual property rights caused by the Service Provider’s Confidential Information or Services;
- Any violation of the Service Provider’s obligations under this Agreement or applicable laws.

customer_indemnification.description:
The Customer shall indemnify, defend, and hold harmless the Service Provider from and against any claims, damages, liabilities, losses, or expenses (including reasonable attorneys’ fees) arising out of or related to:
- Any breach of the Customer’s warranties under Section [X];
- Any infringement of third-party intellectual property rights caused by the Customer’s Confidential Information or Data;
- Any violation of the Customer’s obligations under this Agreement or applicable laws.

survival.provisions:
